method.description:
Submits a task returning a [HEGoPointOutput]: the cooked output, read and split from code rather than through a fetch configuration.

Pass [code]preload_attribs[/code] to have those point attributes loaded while the task runs, so no further await is needed before querying:
[codeblock]
var output = await agent.task(asset_node.get_point_output(["N", "up", "hego_spawn"]))
for group in output.filter_by("hego_spawn", 1).split_by("hego_node_path").values():
    var points = group.get_points(["N", "up"])
[/codeblock]

Attribute values are cached per cook and shared with [method fetch_points] and [method fetch_surfaces], so reading the same attribute twice only reaches Houdini once.

Submits a task returning a [HEGoSurfaceOutput]: the cooked surfaces, read and split from code rather than through a fetch configuration.

[code]point_attribs[/code] names which of [code]N[/code], [code]Cd[/code], [code]uv[/code], [code]uv2[/code] and [code]tangents[/code] to read; [code]P[/code] always comes along. [code]preload_attribs[/code] are primitive attributes, loaded while the task runs so the queries afterwards need no further await:
[codeblock]
var output = await agent.task(asset_node.get_surface_output(["N", "uv"], ["hego_material"]))
for material in output.split_by("hego_material"):
    var surface = by_material[material].get_surface()
[/codeblock]

[code]custom_attribs[/code] names up to four point attributes, in channel order, that each surface carries as [constant Mesh.ARRAY_CUSTOM0] to [constant Mesh.ARRAY_CUSTOM3], packed to RGBA float per vertex (float or int, tuple size 1 to 4; missing components are 0). A blank name, or an attribute the cook does not have, leaves that channel out. Surfaces with custom channels also hold [code]custom_format_flags[/code], the flags argument [method ArrayMesh.add_surface_from_arrays] needs to add them; [method HEGoMeshOutput.build_array_mesh] passes it.

Attribute values are cached per cook and shared with [method fetch_surfaces] and [method get_point_output].
